  "goodToKnow": "Involvieren means to involve and is mostly used in the passive participle: in etwas involviert sein (to be involved in something), often a scandal or crime. It's a Latin loanword and sounds somewhat formal or trendy; native German alternatives are beteiligt sein (to take part), verwickelt sein (to be entangled) and einbeziehen (to include). The v is pronounced like English v. Perfect without ge-: hat involviert."
